#set heading(numbering: none)

= Terms

*Subject anchored* -- Implemented: coordinates are expressed under the declared subject-level anchoring contract. Interpretation: within-subject task contrasts are meaningful under that contract. Not established: a common between-subject amplitude scale.

*Chart-Jacobian alpha* -- Implemented: spectral abscissa of the local chart Jacobian. Interpretation: a local chart-flow summary. Not established: an identified one-step or biological generator.

*One-step L2/L3* -- Implemented: quantities of an identified lag-1 transition map, reported only where support is available. Interpretation: a model-conditional short-step summary. Not established: the chart Jacobian or an iterated L4 map.

*Reachability amplitude* -- Implemented: a finite-horizon certificate-derived amplitude summary. Interpretation: conditional on certificate validity. Not established: occupancy, dimensional capacity, or causal accessibility.

*BH family* -- The finite tests corrected together by Benjamini--Hochberg. This article keeps occupancy/MNJ/L1/L4 separate from the Jacobian-alpha/L2/L3 panel.

*Partial support* -- The estimator is absent for some recordings because its stated identification/support condition was not met. It is not a zero and not automatically missing at random.
